   "value": "**Result — classes** (L = 2, 3, 4): all three 4, 8, 20; LR only 0, 0, 4; P only 2, 10, 40; LP only 0, 4, 20; none 0, 4, 68. **Q-language, exact for all 184 states (with fixed c):**\n\n| symmetry | eigenvalues | Q-functions |\n|---|---|---|\n| LR (𝒫) | τ̄₁(u) = τ̄₃(u + h) | Q₁(u) ∝ Q₁₂₃(u + h) |\n| P (𝒬) | τ̄₁(u) = τ̄₁(2h − u) | Q₁(u) ∝ Q₁₂₃(2h − u) |\n| LP (𝒫𝒬) | τ̄₁(u) = τ̄₃(3h − u) | Q₁(u) ∝ Q₁(h − u) |\n\n(Reflection u → c−u turns the Baxter equation into the dual one, so parity exchanges Q₁ ↔ Q₁₂₃; composed with LR it maps Q₁ to itself.)\n\n## Part 2: product states preserving P or LP (L = 2, exact)\n\nLeft kernels of X_P(u) = t̄₁(u) − t̄₁(2h−u) and X_LP(u) = t̄₁(u) − t̄₃(3h−u); product-state search as in `abjm-LR-factorized.wb`. Twisted: first count symmetric states for the LR-compatible twist Λ = diag(z₁, z₂, 1/z₂, 1/z₁) and for a generic diagonal twist.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[ee, rho, siteOpL, lax1, lax3, mono, transferM, prodVec];\nnn = 4;\nee[i_, j_] := SparseArray[{{i, j}} -> 1, {nn, nn}];\nrho[\"A\"][i_, j_] := ee[i, j]; rho[\"F\"][i_, j_] := -ee[j, i];\nid4 = IdentityMatrix[nn, SparseArray];\nsiteOpL[s_, m_, L_] := KroneckerProduct @@ Table[If[b == s, m, id4], {b, L}];\nlax1[ty_][v_, t_][i_, j_] := (v - t) KroneckerDelta[i, j] id4 + hh rho[ty][i, j];\nlax3[\"A\"][v_, t_][k_, l_] := (v - t + hh) KroneckerDelta[k, l] id4 - hh ee[l, k];\nlax3[\"F\"][v_, t_][k_, l_] := (v - t - 3 hh) KroneckerDelta[k, l] id4 + hh ee[k, l];\nmono[lax_, types_, ths_, v_] := Module[{L = Length[types], T},\n   T = Table[siteOpL[1, lax[types[[1]]][v, ths[[1]]][i, j], L], {i, nn}, {j, nn}];\n   Do[T = Table[Sum[T[[i, k]] . siteOpL[s, lax[types[[s]]][v, ths[[s]]][k, j], L], {k, nn}], {i, nn}, {j, nn}], {s, 2, L}]; T];\ntransferM[lax_, types_, ths_, v_, G_] := With[{T = mono[lax, types, ths, v]}, Sum[T[[i, j]] G[[j, i]], {i, nn}, {j, nn}]];\ntypes4 = {\"A\", \"F\", \"A\", \"F\"}; thAB4 = {2 hh, 0, 2 hh, 0};\nprodVec[x_List] := Module[{c = x[[1 ;; 16]] + I x[[17 ;; 32]]}, Flatten[Outer[Times, Sequence @@ Partition[c, 4]]]];\n(* kernel of a polynomial operator X(u) (left kernel), product search and classification *)\nleftKernel[Xu_] := Module[{Xm = Normal[Expand[Xu]], dg, Xk}, dg = Max[Exponent[Flatten[Xm], u]]; Xk = Table[Coefficient[Xm, u, k], {k, 0, dg}]; NullSpace[Join @@ (Transpose /@ Xk)]];\nprodSearch[Kb_, T1n_, nStart_, seed_] := Module[{Kon = Orthogonalize[N[Kb]], f, runs, zeros, ev, V},\n   f[x_?(VectorQ[#, NumericQ] &)] := With[{b = prodVec[x]}, 1 - Total[Abs[Conjugate[Kon] . b]^2]/Norm[b]^2];\n   SeedRandom[seed];\n   runs = Table[Module[{x0 = RandomReal[{-1, 1}, 32], sol, xs}, sol = Quiet[FindMinimum[f[xs], {xs, x0}, Method -> \"QuasiNewton\", MaxIterations -> 3000]]; {sol[[1]], xs /. sol[[2]]}], {nStart}];\n   zeros = Select[runs, #[[1]] < 10^-12 &];\n   {Length[runs], Length[zeros], Count[runs[[All, 1]], s_ /; s > 10^-6],\n    Tally[Table[With[{b = Normalize[prodVec[z[[2]]]]}, With[{lam = b . T1n . Conjugate[b]/(b . Conjugate[b])}, Norm[b . T1n - lam b] < 10^-6]], {z, zeros}]],\n    Union[Table[Map[Round[#, 0.01] &, Abs[Normalize /@ Partition[z[[2, 1 ;; 16]] + I z[[2, 17 ;; 32]], 4]], {2}], {z, zeros}]]}];\nClear[u];\nKP = leftKernel[transferM[lax1, types4, thAB4, u, IdentityMatrix[nn]] - transferM[lax1, types4, thAB4, 2 hh - u, IdentityMatrix[nn]]];\nKLP = leftKernel[transferM[lax1, types4, thAB4, u, IdentityMatrix[nn]] - transferM[lax3, types4, thAB4, 3 hh - u, IdentityMatrix[nn]]];\nT1n0 = N[transferM[lax1, types4, thAB4, 0.37, IdentityMatrix[nn]]];\nresP = prodSearch[KP, T1n0, 40, 7]; resLP = prodSearch[KLP, T1n0, 40, 8];\nGrid[{{\"\", \"dim kernel\", \"# starts\", \"# zeros\", \"# stuck (f > 10⁻⁶)\", \"zeros: eigen-bra? (tally)\", \"zero types |v_s| (rounded)\"},\n  {\"P, untwisted\", Length[KP], Sequence @@ resP[[1 ;; 4]], Length[resP[[5]]]}, {\"LP, untwisted\", Length[KLP], Sequence @@ resLP[[1 ;; 4]], Length[resLP[[5]]]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
