  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result:** neither link pattern is sufficient. Closer inspection of the L = 2 LP solutions: the **whole A·F pairing matrix vanishes**, v_A·v_F = 0 for every A site and every F site (span(v_A) ⟂ span(v_F), bilinear). Up to GL(4) this is A sites ∈ span(e₁, e₂), F sites ∈ span(e₃, e₄): the **SU(2)×SU(2) sector**, where all K terms vanish. (Earlier χ values were normalised by a vanishing pairing and are meaningless.)\n\n### Check: random product states in the SU(2)×SU(2) sector, and two-site states in it, L = 2, 3, 4",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "sectorState[LL_, seed_, twoSite_] := Module[{v}, SeedRandom[seed];\n   v = If[twoSite, Flatten[Table[{Join[RandomComplex[{-1 - I, 1 + I}, 2], {0, 0}], Join[{0, 0}, RandomComplex[{-1 - I, 1 + I}, 2]]}, 1], 1], Null];\n   v = If[twoSite, With[{a = Join[RandomComplex[{-1 - I, 1 + I}, 2], {0, 0}], f = Join[{0, 0}, RandomComplex[{-1 - I, 1 + I}, 2]]}, Flatten[Table[{a, f}, LL/2], 1]],\n     Table[If[OddQ[s], Join[RandomComplex[{-1 - I, 1 + I}, 2], {0, 0}], Join[{0, 0}, RandomComplex[{-1 - I, 1 + I}, 2]]], {s, LL}]];\n   Flatten[Outer[Times, Sequence @@ v]]];\nsecTest[LL_, kind_, twoSite_] := Max[Table[Module[{B = sectorState[LL, sd, twoSite], rs, us = {0.37, -0.61, 1.13}}, SeedRandom[200 + sd];\n     rs = Table[RandomComplex[{-1 - I, 1 + I}, nn^LL], 2];\n     Max[Flatten[Table[With[{y = Xop[kind, LL][uu, r]}, Abs[B . y]/(Norm[B] Norm[y])], {uu, us}, {r, rs}]]]], {sd, 3}]];\nsecRows = Flatten[Table[{LL/2, If[ts, \"two-site in sector\", \"generic in sector\"], Sequence @@ (ScientificForm[secTest[LL, #, ts], 2] & /@ {\"P\", \"LP\", \"LR\"})}, {LL, {4, 6, 8}}, {ts, {False, True}}], 1];\nGrid[Prepend[secRows, {\"L\", \"product state (A ∈ span(e₁,e₂), F ∈ span(e₃,e₄))\", \"X_P\", \"X_LP\", \"X_LR\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
